 "body": "<link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"../assets/css/article-tables.css\"><p><em>Part 1 of 4 in the inventory control series.</em></p>\n<p>Most warehouses manage every item the same way. The $62 case of gloves that sells 100 times a week gets the same count schedule, the same reorder routine and the same attention as the box of blades that sells twice a week.</p>\n<p>That feels fair, but it is expensive. The buyer's time is spread thin across hundreds of items, so the few that drive the business get no more care than the many that barely matter. The usual result is stockouts on the fast movers and cash tied up in the slow ones.</p>\n<p>ABC analysis fixes this with one afternoon of spreadsheet work. It sorts your inventory into three classes, so you can put tight control where the money is and simple rules everywhere else. This post explains the method and walks through a full example for a distributor.</p>\n<h2>What ABC analysis is</h2>\n<p>ABC analysis ranks inventory items by how much money flows through each one in a year, then splits the ranked list into three classes. It applies the Pareto principle: a small share of items accounts for a large share of the value.</p>\n<p>The measure is <strong>annual dollar usage</strong>: units sold or consumed in a year, multiplied by unit cost. A cheap item that moves in huge volume can outrank an expensive item that rarely moves.</p>\n<table>\n<tr><th style=\"white-space:nowrap\">Class</th><th style=\"white-space:nowrap\">Share of items</th><th>Share of annual dollar usage</th><th style=\"white-space:nowrap\">In plain terms</th></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">A</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">10 to 20%</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">70 to 80%</td><td>The few items that carry the business</td></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">B</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">About 30%</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">15 to 25%</td><td>The middle: important, but not critical</td></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">C</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">50 to 60%</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">About 5%</td><td>The long tail of low-value items</td></tr>\n</table>\n<p>These ranges are guides, not rules. Your own split depends on your product mix, and the goal is a useful grouping, not a perfect 80/20.</p>\n<h2>How to do it in five steps</h2>\n<p>You need a spreadsheet and two numbers per item: units used in the last 12 months, and unit cost.</p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Pull the data.</strong> Export every stocked item with its 12-month usage and current unit cost. Use a full year so seasonal items are not misjudged.</li>\n<li><strong>Calculate annual dollar usage.</strong> Multiply usage by unit cost for each item.</li>\n<li><strong>Rank.</strong> Sort the list from highest annual dollar usage to lowest.</li>\n<li><strong>Add the cumulative percentage.</strong> Work out each item's share of the total, then add a running total down the list.</li>\n<li><strong>Assign classes.</strong> Set your cut-offs and label each item. A common starting point is A up to 80% of cumulative value, B from 80% to 95%, and C for the rest.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>Use cost, not selling price, because the aim is to manage money tied up in stock. If your costs are unreliable, fix the worst of them first; the ranking is only as good as the data behind it.</p>\n<h2>A worked example: a 20-item distributor</h2>\n<p>Northshore Supply is a fictional distributor of packaging and safety products. It stocks 20 items with a combined annual usage of $1,413,000 at cost. The table shows all five steps completed: usage and cost pulled, dollar usage calculated, items ranked, cumulative share added, and classes assigned.</p>\n<table class=\"t-wide\">\n<tr><th>Rank</th><th>SKU</th><th>Item</th><th>Annual units</th><th>Unit cost</th><th>Annual usage</th><th>% of total</th><th>Cumulative %</th><th>Class</th></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">1</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">NS-101</td><td>Nitrile gloves, case of 1,000</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">5,200</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">$62.00</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">$322,400</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">22.8%</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">22.8%</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">A</td></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">2</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">NS-102</td><td>Stretch wrap, 18 in x 1,500 ft</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">9,800</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">$24.50</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">$240,100</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">17.0%</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">39.8%</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">A</td></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">3</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">NS-103</td><td>Corrugated box, 18x12x12, bundle of 25</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">7,400</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">$28.00</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">$207,200</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">14.7%</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">54.5%</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">A</td></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">4</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">NS-104</td><td>Safety glasses, box of 12</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">3,100</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">$54.00</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">$167,400</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">11.8%</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">66.3%</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">A</td></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">5</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">NS-105</td><td>Packing tape, case of 36</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">2,600</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">$38.00</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">$98,800</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">7.0%</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">73.3%</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">A</td></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">6</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">NS-106</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">Degreaser, 20 L pail</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">820</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">$96.00</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">$78,720</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">5.6%</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">78.9%</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">A</td></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">7</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">NS-107</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">Pallet strapping kit</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">410</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">$165.00</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">$67,650</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">4.8%</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">83.7%</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">B</td></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">8</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">NS-108</td><td>Hi-vis vest, pack of 10</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">900</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">$68.00</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">$61,200</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">4.3%</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">88.0%</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">B</td></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">9</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">NS-109</td><td>Absorbent pads, bale of 100</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">760</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">$72.00</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">$54,720</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">3.9%</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">91.9%</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">B</td></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">10</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">NS-110</td><td>Hand cleaner, 4 L, case of 4</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">640</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">$58.00</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">$37,120</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">2.6%</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">94.5%</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">B</td></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">11</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">NS-111</td><td>Shop towels, case of 12 rolls</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">520</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">$44.00</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">$22,880</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">1.6%</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">96.1%</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">C</td></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">12</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">NS-112</td><td>Bubble wrap, 24 in x 250 ft</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">300</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">$36.00</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">$10,800</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">0.8%</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">96.9%</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">C</td></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">13</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">NS-113</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">Ear plugs, box of 200</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">260</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">$32.00</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">$8,320</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">0.6%</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">97.5%</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">C</td></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">14</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">NS-114</td><td>Utility knife, pack of 10</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">190</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">$41.00</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">$7,790</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">0.6%</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">98.0%</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">C</td></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">15</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">NS-115</td><td>Shipping labels, roll of 1,000</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">420</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">$17.50</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">$7,350</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">0.5%</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">98.5%</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">C</td></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">16</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">NS-116</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">Dust masks, box of 50</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">330</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">$19.00</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">$6,270</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">0.4%</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">99.0%</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">C</td></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">17</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">NS-117</td><td>Floor marking tape, roll</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">240</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">$22.00</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">$5,280</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">0.4%</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">99.4%</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">C</td></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">18</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">NS-118</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">Zip ties, bag of 1,000</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">180</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">$24.00</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">$4,320</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">0.3%</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">99.7%</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">C</td></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">19</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">NS-119</td><td>Spray bottles, case of 12</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">110</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">$27.00</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">$2,970</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">0.2%</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">99.9%</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">C</td></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">20</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">NS-120</td><td>Replacement blades, pack of 100</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">95</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">$18.00</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">$1,710</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">0.1%</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">100.0%</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">C</td></tr>\n</table>\n<p>The cut-offs used are 80% and 95% of cumulative value. Plotted as a Pareto chart, the pattern is easy to see.</p>\n<figure style=\"overflow-x:auto\"><svg role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Pareto chart of 20 items ranked by annual dollar usage. Six class A items carry 78.9% of the total, four class B items carry 15.6% and ten class C items carry 5.5%. The cumulative line crosses 80% after the sixth item and 95% after the tenth.\" viewBox=\"0 0 720 400\" width=\"720\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0 auto;min-width:560px\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" font-family=\"Inter,system-ui,sans-serif\" font-size=\"12\"><text x=\"58\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#0B2A5A\">6 of 20 items carry 79% of annual dollar usage</text><text x=\"58\" y=\"46\" fill=\"#5A6475\">Bars: annual value per item, ranked. Line: cumulative share of the $1,413,000 total.</text><line x1=\"58\" x2=\"654\" y1=\"330.0\" y2=\"330.0\" stroke=\"#E3E6EC\"/><text x=\"50\" y=\"334.0\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#5A6475\">$0</text><line x1=\"58\" x2=\"654\" y1=\"259.9\" y2=\"259.9\" stroke=\"#E3E6EC\"/><text x=\"50\" y=\"263.9\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#5A6475\">$100k</text><line x1=\"58\" x2=\"654\" y1=\"189.8\" y2=\"189.8\" stroke=\"#E3E6EC\"/><text x=\"50\" y=\"193.8\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#5A6475\">$200k</text><line x1=\"58\" x2=\"654\" y1=\"119.7\" y2=\"119.7\" stroke=\"#E3E6EC\"/><text x=\"50\" y=\"123.7\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#5A6475\">$300k</text><line x1=\"58\" x2=\"654\" y1=\"149.2\" y2=\"149.2\" stroke=\"#8A93A3\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 4\"/><text x=\"660\" y=\"153.2\" fill=\"#5A6475\">80%</text><line x1=\"58\" x2=\"654\" y1=\"115.3\" y2=\"115.3\" stroke=\"#8A93A3\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 4\"/><text x=\"660\" y=\"119.3\" fill=\"#5A6475\">95%</text><rect x=\"62.0\" y=\"104.0\" width=\"21.8\" height=\"226.0\" fill=\"#0B6FA4\"><title>NS-101 Nitrile gloves, case of 1,000: $322,400 a year, class A</title></rect><text transform=\"rotate(-45 76.9 344)\" x=\"76.9\" y=\"344\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#5A6475\">NS-101</text><rect x=\"91.8\" y=\"161.7\" width=\"21.8\" height=\"168.3\" fill=\"#0B6FA4\"><title>NS-102 Stretch wrap, 18 in x 1,500 ft: $240,100 a year, class A</title><